Z||000009||turbo86se||02-01-2001||12:57 PM||||Unless it's a Sunday, I can't go anywhere until April. By then, hopefully, I'll have the coupe running, but how long have I been saying that. <P>Of course, you guys are welcome to come up and get the turbo!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||2birds||02-01-2001||09:31 PM||||According to the ad in Hemmings Motor News, Moultrie is just south and west of Tifton, a bit west of I-75.  Tifton is about an hour north of the FL/GA line on I-75.  <BR>It is a swap meet and Car Corral.  My friend, who goes every year, says that it has a little bit of everything car related, and is better than either Daytona meet, in his opinion.  The ad says it is the 25th annual meet, and it is sponsored by a Pontiac Dealer.  It is on an old airfield, with lots of old hangars for indoor vendor setup in case of rain.<P>I've never been, but I'm going to miss the Daytona meet, so I'll try it out.  I've been to Daytona, Carlisle, Hershey, and Iola swap meets, so I'll have something to compare it to.<P>It opens at 8 on Fri, Sat and Sun<P>If nothing else, it gets me a chance to spend a couple hours in my GT...<p>[This message has been edited by 2birds (edited 02-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||2birds||02-02-2001||12:31 PM||||On another note, I found out who got the 86 GT that was sold from a dealer here in Kingsland a few weeks ago.  He's on a boat here, and I hooked up with him for a bit this morning.  His car is pretty clean, with 78,000 miles, but it was badly neglected mechanically (brakes, struts/shocks, egr diaphragm is broken off, alignment, no recalls ever done from the looks of it, cracked rear exhaust manifold, and a few electrical gremlins to rear their ugly heads.  <BR>I told him about the Forum and the N FL/SE GA group.  Our sea-going schedules don't exactly work too well right now, but I offered to help him as much as I can.  I told him to run the VIN at Bennet Chevrolet for recall info, and to get the brakes and alignment done first, since the budget is getting tighter.  He already started brakes at Olson Tire, but they told him he needs a new master cylinder, too, because the rears are doing most of the work now.  ||||reg||1
